  "helpTitle": "Help",
  "faq1q": "What is \"can spend\"?",
  "faq1a": "Money in the counted accounts, minus planned bills until the end of the period (including overdue), minus open card statements, minus reserves kept inside accounts and the cushion you set. Planned income only counts in optimistic mode. It is an estimate, not a balance.",
  "faq2q": "Does a card purchase count twice?",
  "faq2a": "No. The purchase is an expense on the date it happened (in its category). Paying the statement only takes money from the account and reduces the statement.",
  "faq3q": "How does the statement work?",
  "faq3a": "Purchases up to the closing day go into the month's statement; after that, the next. Installments fall one per statement. The due date is the day you registered.",
  "faq4q": "What is today's mark?",
  "faq4a": "On budget bars, the mark shows where spending would be today if spread evenly over the days of the month. Before it: within plan. Up to 10 points after: slightly above. Beyond that or over the limit: above plan.",
  "faq5q": "Planned × settled",
  "faq5a": "Planned is what is still to happen (bill to pay, salary to receive). Settled already happened and changes the balance. A partial payment stays \"partial\" until complete.",
  "faq6q": "Reserves and goals",
  "faq6a": "Saving money into a goal takes the amount from the source account. If the goal sits inside a counted account, the saved amount is deducted from \"can spend\" (when protected).",
  "faq7q": "Loans",
  "faq7a": "Price table (fixed installment) or SAC (decreasing installment), with a monthly rate on the outstanding balance. \"Pay off today\" is the present value of the remaining installments at the contract rate, no fees: an estimate for negotiating.",
  "faq8q": "Supermarket",
  "faq8a": "A barcode identifies the product, not the price. The price comes from the scanned tag (OCR), your history or you. Nothing is added without confirmation, and the cart total uses scale rounding.",
  "faq9q": "My data",
  "faq9a": "Everything stays on the device, encrypted. Export backups in the menu, under Export and backup. Erase everything in Privacy.",
